  "scenario": "Use the MDIO-lock kernel and one unlocked Plasma session. Route the EQOS interrupt to CPU0, then CPU6, then CPU0 with intrctl. Run 10-second TCP streams and 300 Mbit/s UDP streams in both directions for each route. Verify the restored interrupt affinity after the last run.",
  "expected": "Compare receive throughput, interrupt rates and UDP loss at each CPU selection, and restore the initial affinity.",
  "observed": "TCP receive throughput measured 787, 927 and 783 Mbit/s in run order. At 300 Mbit/s, UDP receive loss measured 1426, 667 and 1086 datagrams. The final interrupt configuration selected CPU0. The desktop session stayed active.",
  "limits": [
    "One pass per CPU setting was measured. The results cover this gigabit link and workload.",
    "The echo sender missed the specified 10 ms pacing in all three runs. They do not establish the effect of the CPU selection on round-trip latency."
  ]
